{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/939700-stranger-things-series-as-shadow-realm-story","id":939700,"title":"Stranger Things series as Shadow Realm story","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-29T12:21:48-07:00","id":939700,"title":"Stranger Things series as Shadow Realm story","content":"<b>Note:</b> This topic is, of course, one big TV series spoiler. If you did not watched new Netflix series yet, just go and see it yourself - you will thank me later.<br /> <br /> And from now on...<br /> <br /> <br /> To me whole concept of 'Upside Down' looks very much as more gloom Shadow Realm. The only real difference is that it's very... empty. Like the Monster is only real dweller of it. Maybe it's just local weirdness of Hawkins town. Just see those.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/bQDTUsU.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/fz4xRPh.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/uMLJ9aO.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/r6v8kJO.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-29-2016, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T12:26:48-07:00","id":939706,"title":"","content":"As we are at him - I think that Monster is some kind of Host - it explains fungal changes near the places he has 'breached' the Gauntlet, literally tearing it for few seconds. It also explains the finale of seasons... Look at him - he could have been sometime before poor man overridden by this <i>shartha</i>.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/yTuCp2U.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/kqAQ2vW.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T12:33:43-07:00","id":939710,"title":"","content":"What even more awesome, <a href=\"http://www.polygon.com/2016/7/22/12236884/stranger-things-netflix-dungeons-and-dragons\" target=\"_blank\">kids in the series are refer 'Upside Down' as <i>Vale of Shadows </i>from their D&amp;D books</a>. They even quote it's description in episode:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Shadows cling to the walls of the canyon, even in the brightest day, and some of the shadows walk, carrying their burden of hatred and hunger with them. Beware this place.&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T08:31:04-07:00","id":940088,"title":"","content":"I agree on all these points <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The Upside-Down definitely made me think of the Shadow whenever I saw it.<br /> <br /> As for the creature itself, I'm torn between it being a <i>shartha</i> or one of the Claimed. Or it could even be some sort of Pangaean Horror along the lines of the creatures found in the third chapter of Predators. If he <i>is</i> one of the former, he certainly wouldn't be an <i>Usudwirku </i>(Fungal Host from Night Horrors: Wolfsbane). Or maybe he could be, and it might be along the lines of the <i>Azarath </i>and other humanoid types of Hosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"user